WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:04.100
Leah: In the past children and young
people who showed signs of severe mental

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:08.969
illness such as Schizophrenia and bipolar
disorder, were thought to be not able to

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:13.520
function properly throughout life and may
never successfully contribute to society.

00:00:14.059 --> 00:00:18.229
However, this is not the case when
handled appropriately with individuals

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:20.210
being involved in their own treatment.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:24.619
Rhiannon: The recovery model is familiar
to most mental health practitioners and

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:29.170
psychologists, psychiatrists, doctors,
and other health professionals can

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:31.209
provide such support to some degree.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:39.566
However, the connections and support
offered by family, friends, and other

00:00:39.566 --> 00:00:43.850
peers can also be critical, along
with support groups and the community.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:48.260
In particular, the recovery
model stresses the importance of

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:50.470
connectedness and social supports.

00:00:50.809 --> 00:00:54.299
When children and young people have
supportive relationships that offer

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.210
unconditional love, they are better
able to cope with the symptoms of their

00:00:58.210 --> 00:00:59.990
illness and work towards recovery.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:04.060
Leah: The recovery model of mental
illness is often contrasted against

00:01:04.069 --> 00:01:05.590
what is known as the medical model.

00:01:06.349 --> 00:01:10.080
The medical model focuses on mental
disorders having physiological

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:13.740
causes, with treatment often
focused on the use of medications.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.710
The two different models are often
presented as being in opposition

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:24.020
to one another, but they can be
complementary and can be used together.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:27.579
Rhiannon: While the medical model
ensures that physiological causes are

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:32.010
fully addressed, the recovery model
ensures that individuals are able to be

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:36.590
directly involved in their own treatment,
offering them personal empowerment,

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:40.729
and the family or peer support needed
to cope with their illness and help

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:42.170
them work towards getting better.

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:46.050
Leah: One of the recovery model’s
major benefits is that it focuses

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:49.040
on the individual’s strengths and
abilities in knowing their own

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:53.530
experiences and to be able to take
an active role in their treatment.

